      "standardized_narrative": "Opening gross claims outstanding at 1 January 2020 were GBP 1,123.995m. Using the syndicate's gross claims development table (cumulative gross claims incurred), estimated prior-year development (years 2018 and older) shows a net adverse reestimate of approximately GBP 24.6m (around 2.19% of opening reserves), i.e. a strengthening of reserves. The syndicate reports significant 2020 impacts from the COVID-19 pandemic (additional gross losses of GBP 201.7m, net GBP 152.7m) and GBP 18.4m of 2020 natural catastrophe losses (Derecho storms and Hurricane Laura). Historic prior-year movements referenced in the report include natural catastrophe-driven net losses in 2016, 2017 and 2018 and higher than expected prioryears' development affecting 2019. The prior-year development figure above is calculated from the published gross claims development triangle and excludes the two most recent underwriting years per the standard methodology.",
